# secrets
.env

# Session details: speaker names, the talk title, the operator's notes. Not
# public, and edited on the day from /admin - sometimes mid-session. The repo
# is public, so the real file is local only and config/session.example.yaml
# is the committed shape. Verified on 2026-10-13 that no version of this file
# with real values has ever been committed.
config/session.yaml

# session artifacts (never committed, never served)
logs/
recordings/
clips/
eval/out/

# python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/

# raw Soniox captures: verbatim transcripts of whatever was recorded.
# Committing one is a deliberate act (git add -f), e.g. into tests/fixtures/.
# The analyzer's markdown reports (docs/captures/*.md) quote the transcript too
# and are tracked on purpose: they are the Phase 1 evidence. Same judgment
# applies before making this repo public.
docs/captures/*.jsonl

# Live-run recordings, same judgment as docs/captures/*.jsonl above: they are
# verbatim transcripts of whatever was said in the room, and run7's includes a
# third-party YouTube clip played aloud. The analysis in docs/live/*.md is
# tracked and quotes only what it needs. Committing a raw one is a deliberate
# act (git add -f).
docs/live/*.jsonl
docs/live/*.json
